meta {
  name: SuperUser - Update Role Setting
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/role-settings/DeptHOD
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "label": "Department Head",
    "description": "Handles requests assigned to the department",
    "isActive": true,
    "sortOrder": 4
  }
}

docs {
  # SuperUser - Update Role Setting

  Changes how one role appears in the Add / Edit User form. The role name in the URL
  must be one of the fixed roles (e.g. `DeptHOD`). All body fields are optional.
  Requires: SuperUser.

  **Display only** — never changes any user's role or permissions.

  ## Body
  | Field       | Description                                   |
  |-------------|-----------------------------------------------|
  | label       | Name shown in the dropdown (required if sent) |
  | description | One-line hint under the dropdown              |
  | isActive    | Show (true) / hide (false) in the dropdown    |
  | sortOrder   | Position in the dropdown (lower = higher)     |

  ## Errors
  | Status | Reason                                         |
  |--------|------------------------------------------------|
  | 400    | Empty label, or trying to show SuperUser       |
  | 404    | Unknown role                                   |
  | 403    | Not SuperUser                                  |
}
